  "body": "Found by adding a warning to wattsi:\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/wattsi/pull/17\n\n[AGIF] and [UNDO] were both used inside comments. The [AGIF] link is\n404, so remove that. Keep [UNDO] for later untangling.\n\nThese are the commits when each reference was last seen in source:\n\n5e99b27 [AES128CTR] Clean up some internal annotations\n61b568a [AGIF] Remove the &lt;img> stuff so that zcorpan can edit it instead.\nf619b0c [ARIAIMPL] reference other documents for ARIA behavior and semantics\nf619b0c [ARIACAAM] reference other documents for ARIA behavior and semantics\na731806 [CP50220] Clean up requirements around encodings\nf5fc01e [CUSTOM] Remove the obsolete integration for custom elements from the HTML spec.\n8d7fe57 [ECMA357] Give JavaScript MIME types a <dfn> to refer to\n11e7419 [EUCKR] Embrace the Encodings specification.\n11e7419 [EUCJP] Embrace the Encodings specification.\nb4cf2fb [FILESYSTEMAPI] Move FileCallback into the spec rather than referencing File System API just for that.\n5984a04 [FORK] Big editorial cleanup. No normative changes.\n11e7419 [GBK] Embrace the Encodings specification.\n70b0ce4 [HATOM] Drop the Atom conversion section entirely.\n5e99b27 [HMAC] Clean up some internal annotations\nfad3534 [HPAAIG] Remove some entries that really aren't helping anyone.\n77db356 [HTML] Try to get things ready for more radical changes.\n9685a53 [IANALINKTYPE] Remove references to the link relations registry\n5e99b27 [ICE] Clean up some internal annotations\nf4cfc37 [IEEE754] defer to WebIDL for how to handle erorneous inputs to th CanvasPixelArray setter.\n9fea997 [NPN] Transferred the Web Sockets Protocol to Ian Fette.\n5fde4b3 [PORTERDUFF] Defer to Rik's spec for globalCompositeOperation\n9fea997 [RFC1321] Transferred the Web Sockets Protocol to Ian Fette.\na731806 [RFC1345] Clean up requirements around encodings\na731806 [RFC1468] Clean up requirements around encodings\nb507eb9 [RFC1494] fax: is apparently no longer in season.\na731806 [RFC1554] Clean up requirements around encodings\na731806 [RFC1557] Clean up requirements around encodings\na731806 [RFC1842] Clean up requirements around encodings\na731806 [RFC1922] Clean up requirements around encodings\n5eaaac1 [RFC2045] Update references to base64\na731806 [RFC2237] Clean up requirements around encodings\n9fea997 [RFC2246] Transferred the Web Sockets Protocol to Ian Fette.\nb507eb9 [RFC2806] fax: is apparently no longer in season.\n9fea997 [RFC4366] Transferred the Web Sockets Protocol to Ian Fette.\n5e99b27 [SDP] Clean up some internal annotations\n5e99b27 [SDPLABEL] Clean up some internal annotations\n5e99b27 [SDPOFFERANSWER] Clean up some internal annotations\n5e99b27 [SHA1] Clean up some internal annotations\n2e01f89 [SHADOW] Add a reference for future use ([SHADOW]).\n11e7419 [SHIFTJIS] Embrace the Encodings specification.\n5e99b27 [STUN] Clean up some internal annotations\n11e7419 [TIS620] Embrace the Encodings specification.\n5e99b27 [TURN] Clean up some internal annotations\n59b7e24 [UCA] Remove table sorting model\nc04640e [UNDO] drop the note about the implications of drag-and-drop on undo\ne73ae63 [WHATWGBLOG] Update references in all the specs I'm working on.\n11e7419 [WIN1252] Embrace the Encodings specification.\n11e7419 [WIN1254] Embrace the Encodings specification.\n11e7419 [WIN31J] Embrace the Encodings specification.\n11e7419 [WIN874] Embrace the Encodings specification.\n11e7419 [WIN949] Embrace the Encodings specification.\nb69fffc [XHTML1] Expand the history section, drop the relationships sections.\nb69fffc [XHTMLMOD] Expand the history section, drop the relationships sections.\n",
